The current Python behavioral reference is reviewed PR #23 head
9cd5b307c328ddc99994561e44e0fff272e83001, pending upstream merge.

Profile inference includes modified JavaScript adaptations of the membership,
property and equality rules in OWL-RL/owlrl 7.1.4 by Ivan Herman and W3C,
https://github.com/RDFLib/OWL-RL. Changes include bounded graph/path expansion
and integration with the required RO-Crate profile. The W3C Software and
Document Notice and License is retained in LICENSES/owlrl.txt.

Model integer coercion includes a modified JavaScript adaptation of
pydantic-core 2.41.5's integer normalization and error boundaries,
https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-core. Its MIT notice is retained in
LICENSES/pydantic-core.txt.

Model date parsing includes a modified JavaScript adaptation of speedate
0.17.0's clock/timezone parsing and exact-date rules, with Pydantic error
classification. https://github.com/pydantic/speedate; MIT notice retained in
LICENSES/speedate.txt.

RDF literal identity and node labels use modified JavaScript adaptations of
RDFLib 7.6.0's numeric/whitespace normalization, scoped-context selection,
namespace binding and N3 URI splitting, Copyright (c) 2002-2026 RDFLib Team,
https://github.com/RDFLib/rdflib. Its BSD 3-Clause license is retained in
LICENSES/rdflib.txt. Normalized terms reach both collection checks and profile
inference.

Node labels and ontology namespace restoration include modified JavaScript
adaptations of pySHACL 0.31.0, by Ashley Sommer,
https://github.com/RDFLib/pySHACL. Its Apache-2.0 license is retained in
LICENSES/pyshacl.txt.

Calendar duration conversion adapts RDFLib's isodate-derived xsd_datetime
arithmetic and formatting. Its additional copyright notices and BSD conditions
are retained in LICENSES/isodate.txt.

HTML literal parsing and serialization adapt html5rdf 1.2.1's strict fragment
boundaries, optional-tag filtering, attribute quoting and token serialization.
Its MIT notice is retained in LICENSES/html5rdf.txt. XML fragment serialization adapts the pinned Python
minidom behavior. Manifest string-list diagnostics use the pinned Python Unicode
printability data and string representation rules; its notice is retained in
LICENSES/CPython.txt. XML and HTML parser dependencies retain their bundled notices.

OWL lexical validation also adapts CPython 3.13.12's _strptime field expressions
and urllib.parse authority checks, using captured Python 15.1 Unicode categories
in JavaScript. The modified checks perform no network access. The Python
Software Foundation notice is retained in LICENSES/CPython.txt.

See LICENSE, LICENSES, dist/third-party.json and dist/licenses for bundled
third-party material. This library is independently packaged.

The TSV reader includes a modified JavaScript adaptation of pandas 3.0.2's
tokenizer and read buffering, Copyright (c) 2012, Lambda Foundry, Inc., except
where noted. It incorporates components of WarrenWeckesser/textreader, licensed
under 3-clause BSD. Numeric conversion also follows pandas. The complete pandas
wheel copyright notices and license are retained in LICENSES/pandas.txt.

Three bundled packages omit license text in their npm archives. Exact-version
license provenance is retained under LICENSES/bundled: @vocabulary/sh includes
the upstream repository's MIT notice; @tpluscode/rdf-ns-builders and clownface
declare MIT in package metadata but supply no license/copyright notice in their
exact upstream trees. Standard MIT permission/warranty text and their declared
author attribution are retained without inventing copyright holders or years.
